      "body": "## Summary\n\nRemoves the hardcoded `trust_remote_code=True` used by the WebUI when loading models/tokenizers. Remote-code execution is now an explicit **server-side opt-in** (`LLAMAFACTORY_WEBUI_TRUST_REMOTE_CODE`, default **off**) and is never derived from the user-supplied model path.\n\n## Finding\n\n| Field | Value |\n| --- | --- |\n| **Name** | Unauthenticated remote code execution in the Gradio WebUI via `trust_remote_code=True` on an attacker-controlled model path |\n| **Severity** | CRITICAL |\n| **CVSS** | 9.8 (CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H) |\n| **Scan ID** | `cmvgxjs4n00kzqn01fnzaqwf5` |\n| **Affected** | `chatter.py:139`, `runner.py:183,329`, `components/export.py:100` |\n\n## PoC summary\n\nThe WebUI launches with no authentication and the model path is a free-text field. An unauthenticated HTTP POST to the Gradio queue join endpoint for the Load-model handler with `model_path` pointing at an attacker-controlled HF-style repo causes `transformers` to import and execute the repo's `configuration_evil.py` **inside the server process** (marker file written on the host). Code executes during config import — before tokenizer/weight loading fails — so no valid model weights are required:\n\n```\nPOST /gradio_api/queue/join  ->  Load-model handler  ->  model_path=<attacker repo>\n                                     |\n                                     +-> transformers imports configuration_evil.py\n                                         => arbitrary Python execution as the WebUI user\n```\n\n## Fix explanation\n\n- Replace each hardcoded `trust_remote_code=True` with `is_env_enabled(\"LLAMAFACTORY_WEBUI_TRUST_REMOTE_CODE\")` (default `0`/off), reusing the existing `is_env_enabled` helper.\n- The opt-in lives on the **server** (env var), so a network client can no longer turn remote-code execution on by choosing a model path.\n- Result: remote code is never executed for a user-supplied path unless the operator explicitly opted in.\n\nFiles changed:\n- `src/llamafactory/webui/chatter.py`\n- `src/llamafactory/webui/runner.py` (train + eval)\n- `src/llamafactory/webui/components/export.py`\n\n## Notes for maintainers\n\nOperators who intentionally rely on remote code (e.g. custom `auto_map` models) can restore the previous behaviour by exporting `LLAMAFACTORY_WEBUI_TRUST_REMOTE_CODE=1`. Consider additionally defaulting the Gradio bind to `127.0.0.1` and adding `launch(auth=...)` for defence in depth.\n\n---\nAutomated security fix by [FailSafe Security](https://getfailsafe.com) — scan `cmvgxjs4n00kzqn01fnzaqwf5`.\n",
